    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: First-Time Visitors Bike Choice</h1>
    <p>Choosing a bike is the first decision of your first Hanoi rental, and it is the decision that quietly shapes everything after it: how confident you feel in traffic, how tired you are at the end of the day, and how much of the city you actually see. First-time visitors tend to choose with their eyes, picking the machine that looks fastest or coolest, when the correct choice is made with an honest assessment of the rider: your experience, your plans and your comfort. This guide walks that assessment in plain language, so your first rental starts on the right machine.</p>
    <p>This article is written for the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> audience of first-time visitors, and it stays on the question of bike choice. Every verified price quoted here lives on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost hub</a>, and the questions that go beyond choosing a bike are answered on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page. Where your plans need terms specific to us, those are agreed directly at booking.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Start with the rider, not the bike</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The automatic question</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">The budget tier: what 150,000 VND buys</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">The premium tier: what 200,000 VND buys</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">City plans versus trip plans</a></li>
